==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|chump||dated}}

===Etymology===
U.S. regional variation of {{m|en|champ#Verb|champ|pos=verb}}, from {{inh|en|enm|champen}}, {{m|enm|chammen|t=to bite; gnash}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/tʃɒmp/}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|chŏmp}}, {{IPA|en|/t͡ʃɑmp/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-chomp.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|chomp}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒmp|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The act of [[chomping]] {{qualifier|see below}}
# {{lb|en|computing|rare}} A unit of computing storage equal to sixteen [[bit]]s, which can [[represent]] any of 65536 distinct values.<ref>{{cite-web | title=Bit Nibble Byte Chomp – a call to action |date=2011-03-22 |blog=trefor.net |author-first=Trefor |author-last=Davies |url=http://www.trefor.net/2011/03/22/bit-nibble-byte-chomp-a-call-to-action/ |quote=The Timico engineering team has started to use the word “chomp” to represent two bytes or the 4 Hex character block in IPv6.}}</ref>
#: {{syn|en|hextet}}
#: {{ux|en|An IPv6 address is represented as eight hexadecimal '''chomps'''.}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[bite]] or [[chew]] [[loudly]] or heavily.
#: ''The dog '''chomped''' on the treat and swallowed it in one gulp.''
# {{lb|en|computing|transitive|[[Perl]]}} To remove the final character from (a [[text]] [[string]]) if it is a [[newline]] (or, less commonly, some other programmer-specified character).
#: {{cot|en|chop}}

